      "point": "Discussion regarding Proposed Ordinance 2026-0108, which authorizes the sale of 39.1 acres of surplus agricultural land in Townsville District 9 (part of King County Water and Land Resources Division/Willard). The property was declared surplus on September 8th, 2021, with an appraised value of $600,000 based on a sales comparison approach. Key concerns include the thirty-year agricultural easement imposed by the state DNR (State Department of Natural Resources) to preserve land use, which is not perpetual. The committee reviewed Amendment one and the motion for council approval.",
