    },
    {
      "point": "Discussion regarding Proposed Ordinance 2026-69 concerning the sale of approximately 180 square feet of county-owned property in Kent, Washington (Clark Lake Park), for an estimated $147,000. The historical context notes that King County acquired Clark Lake Park with state grant funding requiring permanent preservation for outdoor recreation. A long-standing unresolved obligation exists from a 1996 Interlocal Agreement (ILA) regarding road widening and replacement land payment, which stalled the transfer of park use to address stormwater drainage issues.",
      "speaker": [
        "yoyoyo",
        "Rod Domowsk",
        "Council Member Fain"
      ],
      "action_owner": null
    },
    {
      "point": "Procedural motions and amendments required for the Clark Lake Park property sale, specifically related to correcting flaws in the Purchase and Sale Agreement (PSA) dated June 10, 2026. Amendments were introduced to extend the council approval period from June 17th to July 24, 2026, ensuring the ordinance is effective by this date to resolve a historical land obligation with the City of Kent.",
      "speaker": [
        "yoyoyo",
        "Rod Domowsk",
        "Council Member Fain"
      ],
      "action_owner": null
    }
  ]
}
